reagent-name-vg-anti-toxin = dylovene
reagent-desc-vg-anti-toxin = Dylovene is a broad-spectrum antitoxin.
reagent-name-vg-bicaridine = bicaridine
reagent-desc-vg-bicaridine = Bicaridine is an analgesic medication and can be used to treat blunt trauma.
reagent-name-vg-kelotane = kelotane
reagent-desc-vg-kelotane = Kelotane is a drug used to treat burns.
reagent-name-vg-dexalin = dexalin
reagent-desc-vg-dexalin = Dexalin is used in the treatment of oxygen deprivation.
reagent-name-vg-inaprovaline = inaprovaline
reagent-desc-vg-inaprovaline = Inaprovaline is a synaptic stimulant and cardiostimulant. Commonly used to stabilize patients.
reagent-name-vg-tricordrazine = tricordrazine
reagent-desc-vg-tricordrazine = Tricordrazine is a highly potent stimulant, originally derived from cordrazine. Can be used to treat a wide range of injuries.
reagent-name-vg-alkysine = alkysine
reagent-desc-vg-alkysine = Alkysine is a drug used to lessen the damage to neurological tissue after a catastrophic injury. Can heal brain tissue.
reagent-name-vg-alkycosine = alkycosine
reagent-desc-vg-alkycosine = A mind stablizing brain bleach.
reagent-name-vg-dermaline = dermaline
reagent-desc-vg-dermaline = Dermaline is the next step in burn medication. Works twice as good as kelotane and enables the body to restore even the direst heat-damaged tissue.
reagent-name-vg-dexalinp = dexalin plus
reagent-desc-vg-dexalinp = Dexalin Plus is used in the treatment of oxygen deprivation. Its highly effective.
reagent-name-vg-cryoxadone = cryoxadone
reagent-desc-vg-cryoxadone = A chemical mixture with almost magical healing powers. Its main limitation is that the targets body temperature must be under 170K for it to metabolise correctly, with an even greater effect at under 95K.
reagent-name-vg-clonexadone = clonexadone
reagent-desc-vg-clonexadone = A liquid compound similar to that used in the cloning process. Can be used to 'finish' the cloning process when used in conjunction with a cryo tube.
reagent-name-vg-paracetamol = paracetamol
reagent-desc-vg-paracetamol = Most commonly know this as Tylenol, but this chemical is a mild, simple painkiller.
reagent-name-vg-oxycodone = oxycodone
reagent-desc-vg-oxycodone = An effective and very addictive painkiller.
reagent-name-vg-tramadol = tramadol
reagent-desc-vg-tramadol = A simple, yet effective painkiller.
reagent-name-vg-synthocarisol = synthocarisol
reagent-desc-vg-synthocarisol = Synthocarisol is a synthetic version of Carisol, a powerful analgesic that used to be found in traditional medicines made from the horn of the now-extinct Space African Rhino. Tragically, the horns also contained an equal amount of Anticarisol, which led to the medical community dismissing the remedies as nothing more than placebo and overlooking this reagent for several centuries.
reagent-name-vg-rezadone = rezadone
reagent-desc-vg-rezadone = A powder derived from fish toxin, this substance can effectively treat genetic damage in humanoids, though excessive consumption has side effects.
